### Muonic X-rays as the Si/YSO stack (the Compton detector) sees them, one job (scripts/muonic_xray_stack.sh runs
### many): sea-level cosmic mu+ and mu- of all energies through the default setup with its Al target, so the stack
### hits hold the X-rays of the muons stopped in the target together with everything else the stack sees.
### Needs the aliases stkSeed, stkEvents, stkDir and stkFile.
### EXPACS mu+ and mu- of 0 - 1000 GeV from a 4 x 4 m plane at z = 112 cm (11 cm above the lead layer), zenith
### < 75 deg, as macro/muonic_xray.mac (which takes only the 0.1 - 2 GeV muons that can stop). Only events with
### energy in the stack are written (/EventFilter 6): its hits stk_* (layer, source, energy, time, position) and
### e_si0-2, e_stack0-1, with the TOF bars bar_*, the capture photons mux_* and where the primary ended (end_*).
### The live time in the run tree is that of all the muons, written or not.

/tof/det/worldSize 420 420 300 cm
/update

/OutputFormat 1
/EventFilter 6
/OutputDirectory {stkDir}
/OutputFile {stkFile}
/gun/seed {stkSeed}
/GeneralParticleSource 2
/tof/cosmic/model expacs
/tof/cosmic/species mu+ mu-
/tof/cosmic/angular all 2 mu+ guan mu- guan
/tof/cosmic/planeCenter 0 0 112 cm
/tof/cosmic/halfX 200 cm
/tof/cosmic/halfY 200 cm
/tof/cosmic/thetaMax 75 deg
/tof/cosmic/energyMin 0 GeV
/tof/cosmic/energyMax 1000 GeV
/run/beamOn {stkEvents}
